WEBVTT

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.950
Come on, Aoba,

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:03.220
your bunk's on top, remember?

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:07.050
Why do I find you sleeping in my bed every morning?

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:15.080
It's probably 'cause I'm too lazy to climb back up the ladder after I get up to go to the bathroom.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:18.620
Not to mention it's so cozy and warm sleeping next to you.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.000
You're silly, Aoba...

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.510
The train's here, Aoba.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.810
Come on, hurry!

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:29.280
What's the big rush?

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:34.610
Let's get in the front car.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:35.570
W-Wait!

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:36.990
Aoba!

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:46.720
Anyway, I liked that cake so much that I ordered two pieces!

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:49.500
Your appetite sure is scary, Aki.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:52.270
Look at that.

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:54.510
That house still has its wind chime out.

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:56.740
You're right.

00:03:56.740 --> 00:03:58.710
I wish they'd be a little bit more consistent with the seasons.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.390
Did you see that?

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:02.160
Huh?

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:03.270
See what?

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:06.050
Couldn't you see inside that house through the gap in the curtains?

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.970
I don't think normal people could.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.790
Not in that split second.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:12.520
Right?

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:19.710
Hang on a minute, Aoba!

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:21.000
Where are you going?

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.670
Hey, Tsukishima.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:27.860
Tsukishima?

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:36.670
<i>I'm sure I saw it.</i>

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.080
<i>There was a robbery taking place!</i>

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.120
<i>The second floor on the corner,</i>

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:50.600
<i>with the wind chime outside...</i>

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:55.930
<i>That one!</i>

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.800
<i>But how can I...</i>

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:03.140
Him?

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.010
Police, open up!

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:11.190
Aoba!

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.360
Where'd you go, Tsukishima?

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:49.100
Thank you so much!

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:51.420
You saved my life!

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:54.560
How can I ever repay you?

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.540
Thank you so much!

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:12.480
It's Senda!

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:13.780
You're right!

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:15.870
We saw the article in the newspaper!

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:17.980
You were so cool!

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:20.890
Thanks.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.590
That's awesome, Keiichiro!

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:25.190
You're our school's—

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:27.490
No, you're the entire town's hero!

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:31.730
It wasn't that big of a deal.

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:33.360
Stop being modest!

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:35.440
You stopped a robber armed with a knife!

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:37.270
That's pretty damn awesome!

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:41.440
But how did you know that there was a robbery going on?

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:44.880
Well, uh, you see...

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.650
You saw it from the train, didn't you?

00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:49.810
Through the small opening in the curtains.

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:53.500
Oh! Yup, that's it exactly.
Through the opening in the curtains.

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:55.660
No way!

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:57.630
You actually saw that from a speeding train?

00:06:57.630 --> 00:06:59.520
In a split second?

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:04.230
It shouldn't be too difficult for an athlete with excellent vision like you, right?

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:07.600
Huh? Oh, yeah, it was real easy.

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:09.240
You here, Senda?

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.030
Yes.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:15.840
The husband of the woman you saved is here to personally
thank you for saving his wife while he was out at work.

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:18.060
Give it up for our hero!

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:19.290
Hip hip hooray!

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:25.980
Hooray!

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:32.900
An athlete with excellent vision, huh...

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:42.810
So fluffy!

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:43.770
They look delicious.

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:47.050
Did you get that for stopping the robbery?

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:48.470
W-What if I did?

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:50.540
This'll take care of me.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:54.140
Come on, that's the one I wanted.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:55.710
Well, I'll leave you to enjoy the rest.

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:57.580
Give it back!

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:00.480
I really wanted that fluffy one, you know!

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:01.550
Senda.

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:17.160
Just as I thought.

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:18.440
What's that supposed to mean?

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:22.710
I'm going to go give these cakes to Tsukishima for you.

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:35.520
Tsukishima!

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:44.910
Take this home with you.

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:45.660
What is it?

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:48.340
Your reward for stopping the robbery.

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:50.550
I just got it from Senda.

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:52.750
T-Thanks.

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:55.840
I'm actually surprised you had this with you.

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:04.120
An earlier visitor had this on him, actually.

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:05.780
An earlier visitor?

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:10.040
<i>Aoba!</i>

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:18.260
Why was he carrying a ball with him?

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:22.470
Was it Kitamura?

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:28.710
That means he noticed the robbery, too, doesn't it?

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:32.080
In that split second, through the window of a moving train...

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:36.760
I see.

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:43.350
I tried on that costume we saw last time,

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:44.950
but it didn't look good on me at all!

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:46.620
What did I tell you?

00:09:52.390 --> 00:09:53.920
You okay?

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:55.860
That scared me!

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:56.430
Geez.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:59.320
Sky blue.

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:16.170
One, two, three, four...

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:15.940
Time for din din, Nomo!

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:18.780
five, six, seven, eight.

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:21.450
Two, two, three, four...

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:22.160
five, six...

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:30.540
You should clean your own desk once in a while, too,

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:34.300
instead of just cleaning Wakaba's all the time.

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:38.810
Whatever.

00:10:57.500 --> 00:10:58.700
My bad!

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:00.150
My hand slipped.

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:01.230
Senda?

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:02.630
Yes, what is it?

00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:04.040
Ow!

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:06.040
Don't slack off with the cleaning, okay?

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:08.010
Okay.

00:11:10.030 --> 00:11:11.290
That punk!

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:14.650
That's quite some aim he's got.

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:18.450
That was a fluke.

00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:21.390
Let Kitamura join the team?

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:22.750
Yeah.

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:26.270
He's taken a detour because of what I did,

00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:28.950
but I'm sure he'll make a great addition.

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:31.660
We ninth-graders are retiring soon, you know.

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:36.250
It wouldn't hurt to let him train with you guys a little, right?

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:39.500
It hurts me to think he's going to waste the time until high school, man.

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:41.400
This guy's no joke, Akaishi.

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:42.670
He's the real deal—

00:11:42.670 --> 00:11:43.680
Too late.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:45.590
No, it's not!

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:47.090
He might not have joined the team,

00:11:47.090 --> 00:11:48.880
but he's been training on his own every day—

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:53.190
I'm saying, you recognized his skills way too late.

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:57.110
All right.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:59.550
You can trust me with Kitamura.

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:02.180
But in return, I've got conditions.

00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:03.330
Conditions?

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:08.270
Don't tell anyone that he's playing baseball until we get to high school, all right?

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:10.900
And one more thing.

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:14.110
I want you to come back to the team as well.

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:16.120
You quit the team,

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:19.310
but <i>you've</i> also been training on your own to make up for it, right?

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:24.750
Makihara and the others will be on the high school team as twelfth-graders, you know.

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:29.010
Are you trying to repeat what happened two years ago?

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:32.960
Don't worry.

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:36.160
I won't drag my feet this time around.

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:38.770
I'll be the one acting first.

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:46.180
It's a rocky road ahead for the high school baseball team.

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:47.430
Yeah.

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:49.820
Probably more than you think.

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:54.680
Great.

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:58.390
Another hole in my home run prize socks.

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:01.820
You'd think they'd at least give out some decent socks, geez.

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:03.720
Oh well.

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:05.530
I guess I'll go win some more.

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:23.620
Does he ever miss?

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:44.230
Here's your home run prize.

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:47.160
I don't need it.

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:48.610
Well, don't mind if I do.

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:53.060
Can you have the machine pitch faster instead?

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:54.540
This isn't helping me practice.

00:13:55.130 --> 00:13:57.110
I'm sorry.

00:13:57.110 --> 00:14:02.440
Our goal is to provide an enjoyable playing field for both children and adults alike.

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:04.990
Feel free to try elsewhere if you're so inclined.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:07.620
Are there any other batting centers nearby?

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:11.920
There sure are.

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:14.760
There's one an hour away, if you take the bus from the train station.

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:18.970
Testy girl.

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:20.670
Right?

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:27.720
Who was that?

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:28.740
Hell if I know.

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:32.750
That guy slugged quite a few home runs just now, huh?

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:37.690
He completely smashed your home run record.

00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:03.750
All right, next.

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:21.060
Fight!

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:29.810
Hey.

00:15:31.810 --> 00:15:33.070
Fight!

00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:51.060
I don't mind,

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:55.320
but why do we have to practice in secret like this?

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:57.770
I don't get why I have to pretend like I'm boxing.

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:01.190
You're our secret weapon, that's why.

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:05.470
Until we're on the high school team, anyway.

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:10.650
You need to learn at least one or two offspeed pitches in the meantime.

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:13.840
A hard ball?

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:14.550
Of course.

00:16:17.570 --> 00:16:19.090
Now, come on!

00:16:19.730 --> 00:16:23.060
Can you take over the café counter for a bit, Aoba?

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:24.030
Okay.

00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:27.810
Boy, am I starving.

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:29.670
I'll take a Napolitan and a cup of coffee.

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:31.130
Coming right up.

00:16:32.390 --> 00:16:34.400
Where's Ichiyo?

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:36.470
She's taking a break, I'm afraid.

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:39.780
I'll... just take a coffee then.

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:41.730
What's that supposed to mean?

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:43.630
Oh, nothing...

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:46.260
Hey, Tsukishima.

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:47.350
Wow.

00:16:47.350 --> 00:16:50.430
I didn't know you helped out at the café, too.

00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:52.650
Welcome. What would you like?

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:55.060
Let's see.

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:58.180
A Napolitan and a cup of coffee.

00:16:58.180 --> 00:16:59.760
I didn't say anything.

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:05.130
I wonder if he's thinking of taking up boxing.

00:17:05.590 --> 00:17:06.630
Who are you talking about?

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:09.070
Who else could it be but Kitamura?

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:11.210
Didn't you know about this?

00:17:12.220 --> 00:17:17.150
Why should I care what some guy who lives close to me wants to do?

00:17:17.150 --> 00:17:18.950
Right, right.

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:21.680
I forgot that you hate that guy.

00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:24.620
Here's your Napolitan.

00:17:26.220 --> 00:17:28.170
<i>This</i> is a Napolitan?

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:29.430
Is there something wrong with it?

00:17:29.430 --> 00:17:34.760
I guess looks don't really matter as long as it tastes all right...

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:48.680
Here it comes.

00:17:49.550 --> 00:17:51.660
Now's your last chance to fold.

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:58.350
And this is the baseball team's clubhouse.

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:14.320
I've seen enough.

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:15.700
Let's close the door. It reeks.

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:17.010
What?

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:21.560
Could you at least clean it up a little?

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:24.480
Oh! Of course we can, yes.

00:18:26.210 --> 00:18:28.500
Who the hell were they?

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:29.420
Like I care.

00:18:47.510 --> 00:18:48.640
What is it?

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:49.640
Oh, nothing.

00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:52.910
I just thought you looked happy for some reason.

00:18:57.630 --> 00:18:59.850
I thought Tsukishima would be happy if she saw this.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:02.880
Did Aoba tell you something?

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:04.620
No.

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:08.890
I'm talking about Tsukishima Wakaba.

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:13.220
Apparently she had a dream once.

00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:17.670
Where I was the catcher and you were pitching

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:20.500
at a jam-packed Koshien.

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:32.000
One more out!

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:48.300
One more out!

00:20:12.580 --> 00:20:15.020
She never told me about that.

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:18.960
She couldn't, even if she wanted to.

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:24.320
She dreamt it on <i>that</i> day.

00:20:26.690 --> 00:20:29.740
I was sweeping the front of the store that day

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:31.970
when Tsukishima stopped in front me, smiling,

00:20:31.970 --> 00:20:34.250
and told me about her dream on her way to camp.

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:41.920
Of course, I knew that I wasn't the star in her dream.

00:20:44.230 --> 00:20:48.690
But I was satisfied just knowing that I had made an appearance.

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:50.890
<i>I'm serious!</i>

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:53.090
<i>You were totally cool!</i>

00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:55.390
<i>You looked awesome as a catcher.</i>

00:20:57.350 --> 00:21:01.270
She repeated it over and over as she was leaving.

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:06.070
Don't tell me that's why you became a catcher in middle school.

00:21:07.090 --> 00:21:08.010
Something wrong with that?

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:12.710
Nope. Not at all.

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:15.460
All right, let's go, Kitamura!

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:16.350
Just Ko is fine.

00:21:16.900 --> 00:21:19.290
All right then, let's ko, Kitamura!

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:21.490
That's not what I meant.

00:23:11.370 --> 00:23:12.230
<i>Hello, everyone.</i>

00:23:12.230 --> 00:23:13.930
<i>Why are you here on New Year's Eve?</i>

00:23:13.930 --> 00:23:15.910
<i>Yay, Ko's here! Make me some porridge.</i>

00:23:15.910 --> 00:23:17.390
I'll<i> make your porridge.</i>

00:23:17.390 --> 00:23:18.780
<i>No, I want Ko to make me some.</i>

00:23:18.780 --> 00:23:19.780
<i>Oh, I see.</i>

00:23:19.780 --> 00:23:21.110
<i>Have it your way, then.</i>

00:23:22.230 --> 00:23:23.190
<i>Oh no.</i>

00:23:23.190 --> 00:23:24.920
<i>Momiji's got a high fever.</i>

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:27.880
<i>Get me some ice and a change of clothes for her.</i>

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:31.760
<i>I'm just not cut out to be a good sister like Waka was.</i>

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:33.290
<i>I don't think that's true.</i>

00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:36.330
<i>Next time, on Cross Game Episode Five:</i>

00:23:36.330 --> 00:23:37.360
<i>Could I Borrow Your Pot?</i>

00:23:37.360 --> 00:23:39.000
<i>What kind of a title is that?</i>
